{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute","id":892270,"title":"Conspiracy: The Merrick Institute","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-16T21:45:01-07:00","id":892270,"title":"Conspiracy: The Merrick Institute","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So this is The Merrick Institute. It's the Conspiracy I'm working on for Beast Masters, the Mortal Remains style Hunter piece addressing Beast. I've also included a signature Tactic of theirs, their Endowment, and some relevant Merits. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Conspiracy: The Merrick Institute</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;Frankenfurter said 'don't dream it, be it'. I don't see why we can't do both.&quot;</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In January 1987, Epsilon Protocol became Strunk Developments. In July 1987, Strunk Developments became Merrick Research. Just about every six months, this United States government shadow organization changes its name and burns all paper trails. They destroy all unnecessary research notes, move facilities, and salt and burn. Researchers only know the bare minimum they have to, and undergo excessive and traumatic debriefings if and when they leave. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This organization, Merrick Research we'll call it even though there's no record of that name existing, exists to tap into the subconscious power of the human mind. Another international group had similar goals, developing a method called the Wintergreen Process. The Merrick practice, which has no formal name, is far more dangerous, far more damaging, but ultimately far more dramatic in its effects. Successful inductees become able to walk through a parallel world borne of human nightmares. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The inductees quickly found true monsters within this nightmare realm. The monster's devastated many of the inductees' minds, and left others dead in the real world. Merrick realized that, if harnessed, these nightmare beasts could be unprecedented, unstoppable weapons in the hand of US military interests. These monsters could turn the tide of war, crippling enemy forces and possibly even heads of state, ensuring United States military supremacy for decades to come. Besides, if they didn't figure this out, someone more dangerous would first, right?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merrick &quot;inducts&quot; children who meet certain very rare criteria in standardized tests filtered through the public school system. When these rare combinations of correct and incorrect results come up, Merrick's surrogates offer parents lucrative scholarship packages, and &quot;enrollment in an elite school&quot;. On occasion, parents who refuse these advances disappear, their children ending up in Merrick laboratories anyway. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The children, usually right on the cusp of adolescence, undergo terrifying chemical, psychological, and physical trials made to force specific and targeted growth inside their brains. These trials often kill the subjects, and almost always leave them permanently damaged on a physical or psychological level. Most remain institutionalized for the entirety of their short lives. Some are inducted into military programs. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">At least, that was the case until 2013. A group of prodigious Merrick teens developed codes to communicate in spite of their cells, organized, and overthrew their captors. This group laid waste to the scientists, the guards, and the bureaucrats responsible for their captivity. Only a couple of scientists were left alive, under promise to help the teens survive with their trauma, and to help them harness their dream skills. They freed all the other teens, but maintained a facility for those in persistent vegetative states thanks to Merrick. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The teens knew the beasts of nightmare, and what terrible things they do to humanity. They swore that despite losing their lives to this travesty, they'd make the most of their circumstances, take responsibility, and destroy these threats. Now, they've divided into loosely organized cells all over North America (and at least a couple have snuck abroad), and they scramble from place to place, building and scrapping the technology to support their cause, as they evade the intelligence community's inevitable approach. They sometimes find new institutions, satellite Merrick groups, and they work to liberate them as well. Now, the group has hundreds of teens and young adults, and a handful of older members, survivors from the first nights of the experiment. Survivors adopted the Merrick name as a way to reclaim their lives. They call themselves the Merrick Institute, despite not being an institute in any formal sense, as a sort of defiant mockery of their past captors.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Enemy</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Beasts are the Merrick dreamers' primary target. While they occasionally hunt others thanks to their general level of awareness, their skills are razor-honed to hunt within dreams. Every Merrick dreamer knows at least one peer dead or comatose thanks to these beasts of legend. Many of the dreamers spent years in a Merrick institution before release, so to say that they've had time to build grudges against these monsters is putting it lightly. Most are obsessed, directing vast repressed anger at them, and will do anything to keep others from suffering the same fate. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sometimes, dreamers run afoul of changelings and other strangeness within dreams. One dreamer found herself abducted by a terrifying, alien entity from beyond her dreams. She eventually escaped, but was forever changed. Her flesh bore the words of the stories she remembered to help her escape. She became even better at traveling within dreamscapes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hunters</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Almost all Dream Warriors suffer some form of disability because of their time in the Merrick laboratories. This usually takes the form of a Persistent Condition. Often, these characters train to fight in nightmares to great success. This is represented with the Dream Avatar Merit (see p. XX).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You were on track for success in life. You had a handful of scholarships to major universities thanks to your mastery with technology. Your science fair project was a rudimentary AI. One day, your parents said you were being sent off to a prestigious institution you\u2019d never heard of. You researched them but found nothing. You fought, but they fought harder. Just when you were investigating emancipation late one night, you fell asleep and woke in a lab. Long story short, now you\u2019re the tech wizard for your cell. You don\u2019t like to talk about what you had to do to get out of the institute. In fact, you don\u2019t like to talk to anyone but your AIs. Your cell gives you breadth, because you\u2019re the best at what you do. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You\u2019re the most optimistic of your group. You grew up an orphan. You were used to neglect and mistreatment. As far as you\u2019re concerned, Merrick just gave you a unique skill that makes you special in a world that\u2019s against you. You act as the heart of your group, keeping their spirits up and their organization tight. More importantly, you know how to survive against all odds. You keep your brothers and sisters fed, clothed, and as comfortable as possible. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You\u2019re the truest dreamer in your cell. During the Merrick experiments, you lost consciousness and never regained it. Your cell keeps you alive and save in the physical world, while you protect them in the nightmare world. You\u2019re an expert on the nightmare, because you live it every day and every night. You couldn\u2019t escape it, so you mastered it. In fact, other cells come to you for your expertise, and even some other Compacts and Conspiracies have reached out for your knowledge. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Factions</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Reformers</b> believe that while the Merrick institute was objectively wrong, the group could benefit from more structured organization. They plan to set up new laboratories to further the cause, most likely outside the United States. A few have proposed micro nations for this plan. So far, the largest contingent of Reformers reside in Canada, where they plan to center a network of laboratories. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Firebrands</b> believe dream warriors cannot turn the Merrick Institute into anything more organized than splinter cells sharing information, tactics, and resources. Of course, the truth is that they\u2019re already past that point. But Firebrands believe in tearing down what little formal structure exists within the Conspiracy. They also favor heavily nomadic cell structure. One group has even bombed an established Reformer safehouse and laboratory (in their defense, they used a diversion to empty the place, first). They admit to the crime, saying that it\u2019s for the greater good. While the Conspiracy at large rejects the action, the lack of formal charter or structure prevents any real consequences for the action. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Fleshists </b>openly reject the call to fight nightmares. While they don\u2019t eschew their gifts with dream navigation, they use these powers to fight more immediate threats. Most monsters exist in planes accessible from the nightmare world, so they can even use their gifts for relatively direct attacks. The Fleshists mostly use their talents for information gathering, though, where they learn the nature of monsters and how to best destroy them. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Status</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merrick Institute members have access to the following advantages with Status in their group.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Even the most loosely affiliated Merrick Institute members learn The Procedure. They gain the Tactic free of charge. If they already have it, this Status dot refunds the Experiences spent. Additionally, they gain access to the Dreamscape Endowment. This is more than most Conspiracies get from their first Status dot, but Merrick Institute members have numerous inherent disadvantages thanks to their history.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 More connected members of the Institute benefit from those ties. They gain Allies (Merrick Institute) \u2022, Contacts (Merrick Institute) \u2022, and a Retainer \u2022 in the institute with this dot. This can add to existing Merits, or refund Experiences spent.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 These members have been around for years, and have saved labs full of inductees. They gain the Easy Out, Easy In Merit (see p. XX) free of cost. If they already have it, refund the Experiences spent. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stereotypes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ascending Ones: They walk roads they don't understand. They are impassioned, but they believe their immense knowledge of other spheres translates to our realm. It doesn't.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ashwood Abbey: They walk the dreamscapes for fun. They're privileged. They don't know the darkness like we do. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Task Force Valkyrie: They're unwitting tools of the machine that enslaved us. You're welcome to pity them until they're turned on us. Then, they become threats worse than the monsters.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">New Tactic: The Procedure </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prerequisites: (all participants) Crafts 1, Intelligence 2, Science 1, Medicine 1 (primary actor) Wits 3, Composure 2, Expression 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Requires:</b> 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Primary Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Composure </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Secondary Dice Pools:</b> Intelligence + Science </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Description:</b> With this series of medical procedures, the primary actor &quot;goes under&quot;, lapsing into unconsciousness and entering the primordial dream. The secondary participants use monitoring technology to see the nightmare world around her, and communications technology to interact with her, coaching her and supporting her efforts. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If successful, secondary actors become linked with the dreamer. With -2 penalties thanks to the relative disconnect between the two worlds, the secondary actors can participate in teamwork actions with the primary actor. Depending on the context, the dreamer can act as the anchor for these actions, or as a supporting character. For example, the dreamer would be considered the anchor if the others were helping her to access a beast's lair. On the other hand, if the team is attempting to build a map of the nightmare realm, she could be a supporting actor as she simply moves around the realm showing the others as they cartograph. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Note that this Tactic requires at least moderate amounts of scrap technology to use. A full laboratory is ideal, but skilled users with an abandoned electronics repair shop or computer reseller can mock up the necessary supplies within an hour. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Organizations: This is the signature Tactic of the Dream Warriors. The Null Mysteriis and the Cheiron Group have adapted their own versions of it, thanks to their medical studies into the metaphysical nature of dreams. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">New Merit: Dream Avatar (\u2022)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effect:</b> Your character\u2019s representation within the world of dreams is more capable than her real world self. When you purchase this Merit, choose two Attribute dots, four Skill dots, or one Attribute dot and two Skill dots. When your character manifests in the dream world, she gains those dots, including any derived traits. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Note that traits lost in the dream world which are derived from dots gained from Dream Avatar are purely conceptual, and are not lost in the real world. For example, if your character normally has Stamina \u2022\u2022, but has Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 in the dream world, she has two health boxes which are marked first in a fight, but do not translate to real world damage when she leaves. Dream Avatar can increase an Attribute or Skill to one dot higher than the normal limit (almost always five dots).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">At Storyteller discretion, you may also take this Merit to represent two Merit dots which can only be used in the dream world. A good example of this would be Fighting Style Merits which your character cannot access in the real world, but she knows within the dream. This is common in the Merrick Institute, where characters train for battles in the nightmare. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You may take this Merit as many times as you\u2019d like. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">New Merit: Ephemeral Fetish (\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effect: </b>Your character possesses an item that no longer exists in the real world. The object was something very important to a person, something that provided comfort, that provided solace, a \u201csecurity blanket\u201d if you will. When lost forever or destroyed, this object became something that exists only within dreams, and now always manifests with your character for whatever reason. Perhaps it was given to her, perhaps it was important to her, or perhaps it\u2019s a strong reminder of someone she\u2019s protecting or lost. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This object has immense potency within the dream. It\u2019s effectively immutable and indestructible. Whatever normal form it would take, add 5 Durability to it, and unless completely destroyed in a turn, it completely fixes itself every turn. If destroyed, it will reappear within a week\u2019s time. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The object grants +3 to all practical uses (in dream logic, see p. XX), including use as a weapon. If used as a weapon, ignore normal penalties for improvised weaponry. For example, a literal security blanket may give +3 to rolls to capture a monster as a net, or rolls to use it to glide safely from a high place. It would also give +3 dice when rolled up and used as a whip. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Groups like the Merrick Institute cherish these items. Many members have Ephemeral Fetishes from their friends who died in the institute\u2019s experiments. Some Ephemeral Fetishes have gone beyond simple fetishes, and are prized by the Aegis Kai Doru (see Dream Relic, p. XX).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">New Endowment: Dreamscape </span></span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Initiates of the Merrick Institute gain access to the Dreamscape Endowment. It allows them to do battle and reshape environments within the nightmare world of beasts, as well as the dream realm that changelings traverse. It does not, however, allow access to these places. Characters must find their own access, often through the Procedure Tactic (see p. XX). </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dreamscape has three separate Merits associated with it. Each is purchased as its own \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Merit. Additionally, hunters can adopt Merits which modify these basic abilities. Each of these Merits has listed prerequisite levels of other Dreamscape Merits. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">These Merits work within any lucid dream, as well as within the beasts\u2019 nightmare realm. This includes dreams brought upon by mages and changelings. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dream Shaping (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Effect: Your character can manipulate the stuff of dreams. With a simple touch, she can mold the ephemera within dream realms as if it were clay. Each successive dot increases upon the manipulation possible. Activating Dream Shaping requires a point of Willpower for the first, second, and third dot abilities. Activation makes them available for the entire scene. The fourth and fifth dots require a Willpower point each time they\u2019re used.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Each ability uses a Intelligence + Manipulation + Dream Shaping dice pool. If used against sentient creatures, they\u2019re contested with Resolve + Stamina. Characters affected by Dream Shaping can remove the effects by spending Willpower. Each Willpower point spent takes an instant action, and removes the effects of a single success. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When using Dream Shaping, the effects apply at a rate of one success per turn. So, if you roll four successes, the transformation takes four turns. This can be slowed to encompass an extended action, for example to reshape something into a piece of art with the Crafts Skill. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Note that in dreams, characters can be manipulated into shapes and forms that might not work logically in the physical world. A character whose body is changed to stone doesn\u2019t die because of the change; she\u2019s just less able to move until the effects are repaired. Also, material properties are generally not as extreme as they could be in the real world. In dreams, you may be able to pick up a terrifyingly radioactive material. So while Dream Shaping doesn\u2019t disallow ludicrous and strange creations, the Storyteller is encouraged to make them plausible within illogical dream logic (see p. XX). </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Enhance: With this ability, your character can embolden and build upon already existing materials. Each success on the activation can increase an object\u2019s Size by one, add one to the amount of damage caused by an item, or add one to the object\u2019s Structure. Two successes can add one to the item\u2019s Durability. An item can only be subject to this ability once per scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022\u2022 Deaden: This ability reverses the effects of Enhance. Each success on the activation can decrease an object\u2019s Size by one, subtract one from the amount of damage caused, or remove one point of Structure. Two successes can remove a level of Durability. Objects cannot be reduced to 0 Size with this ability. An item can only be subject to this ability once per scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 Reshape: This ability allows your character to mold objects. She can reshape, shift, bend, and twist objects like they were malleable clay. She cannot change a liquid into a gas or solid, but she can adjust their basic density and hardness. She could make steel a softer metal, or she could make wood hard as a rock; this is functionally identical to five successes on Enhance or Deaden. She can manipulate 1 Size worth of an object per success. If reshaping a character, each success can add ore remove a dot of an Attribute.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Create: This ability works like Reshape, but allows your character to create the initial material to manipulate. The successes determine the initial Size of the object. Creating an object takes a point of Willpower. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Destroy: Using Destroy takes a point of Willpower per use. This ability removes the limitation of Deaden, and cannot be used on an object subject to Deaden in the same scene. If an object would be reduced to Size 0, it is destroyed entirely. When used against a sentient being, the victim\u2019s successes on the contested roll reduce your rolled successes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dream Shield (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Effect: Your character\u2019s mind is steeled against the terrible things that exist within dreams. Each dot of this Merit adds 1/1 armor for the purpose of protecting her against threats in the dreamscape. Additionally, any time she spends Willpower to add -2 to a resistance or +3 to a contested dice pool against Dread Powers in the nightmare, also add her dots to the effect. For example, with three dots, she\u2019d give -5 to resisted rolls, or add +6 to her contested rolls when spending Willpower. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dream Sword (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Effect: Your character\u2019s mind is a weapon in the dream world. Spend a point of Willpower to activate Dream Sword. She has two options; she can create a Size 1 - 3 physical weapon that must be wielded with the Weaponry Skill (or the Brawl Skill if appropriate to the weapon chosen), or she can project an attack at anything within eyeshot with a Wits + Athletics roll. If she uses the former, the weapon persists for the scene, and she cannot be disarmed. If she uses the latter, the weapon works only once, and costs additional Willpower for each additional attack. The weapon has a damage rating equal to your character\u2019s dots in Dream Sword, and can take any physical appearance she wishes. Many members of the Merrick Institute train with martial arts, simply turning their hands and feet into weapons within the dream.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Absorb and Fortify (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Dream Shaping 3, Dream Shield 1 (Dream Sword 1 for \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effect: </b>Your character can not only reshape dreams and defend herself, she can simultaneously do both by absorbing the dreamstuff into herself. When using Dream Shaping to remove Durability or Structure from an object, add her successes as temporary Health boxes. When she takes damage, it\u2019s first applied to these Health boxes, which are removed and cannot be replenished. She cannot \u201cstack\u201d these Health boxes; additional uses of Absorb and Fortify only add additional Health if her successes exceed her current temporary Health, and then she only gains up to her successes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">With three dots, you may also use Absorb and Fortify when using a Dream Sword attack. Successes cause one fewer damage than normal, but also add temporary Health as above. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Colossus (\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Dream Shaping \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effect: </b>Normally, your character can only create relatively human-sized objects, or make large objects somewhat larger with Dream Shaping. With this modification, your character can create massive structures in seconds. When using Dream Shaping to create or grow non-sentient objects, each success adds 3 Size instead of 1. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Regenerative Mind (\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effect:</b> When your character spends Willpower on Dreamscape abilities, she regains one of those spent Willpower every ten minutes. By taking a point of bashing damage reflexively, you can speed this up and immediately replenish one Willpower point. Note that this only works on Willpower spent on Dreamscape abilities.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Shielding Mind (\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Dream Shield \u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effect:</b> Your character can use Dream Shield on another character by spending a point of Willpower. That character gains access to your character\u2019s Dream Shield. He must spend his own Willpower for the contested and resisted effects.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Warp (\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Dream Shaping \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effect:</b> With this modification to Dream Shaping, your character\u2019s Dream Shaping effects occur instantly, regardless of the successes rolled. In fact, her Dream Shaping may be used reflexively when used against inanimate objects.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wrack (\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Dream Sword \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effect: </b>When your character successfully strikes with a Dream Sword attack, you can choose to remove damage from the weapon in order to drain an Attribute from the victim for the scene. By removing three damage from the weapon, you can reduce an Attribute by one dot. By removing five damage from the weapon (requiring five dots in Dream Sword), you can reduce an Attribute by two dots, or two Attributes by one dot. Choose these Attributes before rolling the Dream Sword attack. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:10:47-07:00","id":892286,"title":"","content":"Brilliant.<br /> <br /> Though part of me is disappointed that Reformers are more prevalent in Canada than they are in Australia considering Dreamtime stuff, but it's easier to walk to Canada than Australia I suppose...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:17:24-07:00","id":892290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892286#post892286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brilliant.<br /> <br /> Though part of me is disappointed that Reformers are more prevalent in Canada than they are in Australia considering Dreamtime stuff, but it's easier to walk to Canada than Australia I suppose...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had the same thought. But I do kind of want them physically closer. <br /> <br /> THAT SAID, I think I'll add mention of an Australian lab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:25:28-07:00","id":892293,"title":"","content":"I really like these guys, they feel quite heroic. I like the dream avatar merit, are the extra dots limited by your trait cap still?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:26:42-07:00","id":892294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892293#post892293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like these guys, they feel quite heroic. I like the dream avatar merit, are the extra dots limited by your trait cap still?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dream Avatar can increase an Attribute or Skill to one dot higher than the normal limit (almost always five dots).&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:31:41-07:00","id":892296,"title":"","content":"Doy, that's what I get for skimming. There go my plans for making a hunter who has 20 strength in the dream world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:41:23-07:00","id":892302,"title":"","content":"Mr. Hill, I stand by what I said in the other thread; you're fighting an uphill battle when it comes to getting me to work anything from Beast into my sphere of inspiration, but this is some really compelling stuff. If anything, it makes me sad we don't have a full book on mortls and Astral weirdness. Very much looking forward to the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T00:16:54-07:00","id":892347,"title":"","content":"Awesome! I was interested in the &quot;Dream Warriors&quot; idea, but the idea that they were experimental test subjects who overthrew their captors* really gives them a solid identity that sells them to me.<br /> <br /> *It will be interesting to see how archetypes like this, not to mention organizations like Cheiron, intersect with Deviant: the ??? when it reveals itself...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T00:33:10-07:00","id":892352,"title":"","content":"Well, this is definitely a very interesting group you put together. It made me think of similar groups that have popped up here (specifically <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>'s KSI21) as well as the little I've come across on that old Orpheus game. With regards to other games, Jack from Mass Effect 2 oddly came to mind.<br /> <br /> All in all, excellent work with this group. Looking forward to seeing what other hunters will come out for Beast Masters.... Though I got to ask, though, is that addition going to be free? Or will we need to pay a little to get it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T00:36:41-07:00","id":892354,"title":"","content":"Nicely walking the knife's edge of 'heroic victim' and 'vengeful nightmare'.<br /> <br /> If I can ever actually get a Changeling playtest going, I'll have to see if I can toss these guys in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-17-2016, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T00:46:11-07:00","id":892359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892352#post892352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is definitely a very interesting group you put together. It made me think of similar groups that have popped up here (specifically <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>'s KSI21) as well as the little I've come across on that old Orpheus game. With regards to other games, Jack from Mass Effect 2 oddly came to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>My baby (though TKR had my blessing to run with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I'm actually having mixed feelings on how best to use KSI 21 as the Dream Warriors have the canonical &quot;pseudoscience - sleep projection&quot; niche now. Is the ghost projection vs astral projection aspect distinguishing enough?<br /> <br /> Or I could go back to an earlier draft of them where &quot;sleepers&quot; were only a small portion of agents, and they were more broadly into ephemeral psi-tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T01:17:06-07:00","id":892379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892352#post892352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is definitely a very interesting group you put together. It made me think of similar groups that have popped up here (specifically <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>'s KSI21) as well as the little I've come across on that old Orpheus game. With regards to other games, Jack from Mass Effect 2 oddly came to mind.<br /> <br /> All in all, excellent work with this group. Looking forward to seeing what other hunters will come out for Beast Masters.... Though I got to ask, though, is that addition going to be free? Or will we need to pay a little to get it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I THINK it'll be slight pay? I believe everyone in the Beast Kickstarter gets it though? I'm not sure; I don't handle that side of things. But I imagine it'll be a slight cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T04:51:31-07:00","id":892422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892293#post892293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like these guys, they feel quite heroic. I like the dream avatar merit, are the extra dots limited by your trait cap still?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the survivors are.<br /> <br /> The people they killed were the kind of hunters that provokes the others to start quoting Nietzsche, if not invoking No True Scotsmen (and knowing it's a logical fallacy-but not caring, since a monster hunter is not supposed to be a metaphorical monster).<br /> <br /> Of course, their freedom also leads to a problem-how they going to recruit new guys? It's not a priority at the moment, but eventually, someone needs to hunt Nightmares, and the current someones are dying off.<br /> <br /> On a note that supports other gamelines, I also notice they may people who find it the easiest to actually ally with their favored prey-all the Begotten have to do is convince them people they already hated (the original overseers of the Institute) are responsible for the deaths of their friends (&quot;<i>We </i>were fighting to remain free-just like you&quot;). Hell, they already have someone who may be a changeling or a fae-touched on their employee rolls. And when it comes out, I can see them as housing a Deviant by nature of what they are-the overseers were already sociopathically unconcerned with ethics in the face of their science project, it doesn't take a genius to imagine one of their subjects being pushed so far their <i>flesh </i>became nightmare as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:00:51-07:00","id":892467,"title":"","content":"I'm going to do a full readthrough of this, like I did for the Japanease ones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Backstory</b><br /> <br /> I liked it. It has a nice 80s/90s conspiracy story feel to it which puts it in the right time frame for teen vs Freddy Kruger stories. This is definitely the thematic vibe you want this group to hit. There are however a couple of notable weaknesses:<br /> <br /> Firstly is the reason why they hunt Beasts. This is a group where members are defined by their backstory. The mental trauma of the experiments and the sense of parental betrayal is going to be an ongoing issue throughout the chronicle, hence the Persistent Condition. Thus the thematics their motivation to fight Beasts has to tie in tightly to the backstory. Right now it feels like the Beasts and the constantly renaming agency are wholly seperate entities, both of whom harmed the Hunters; and the constantly renaming agency is by far the larger influence which gives the impression that a chronicle playing the Merrik Institute should be about fighting government conspiracies first and Beasts second. I think that separation needs to be bridged in order to make fighting Beasts more thematically central.<br /> <br /> For example. They might believe that intelligence/espionage community is being preyed upon by Beasts who's lessons of fear teach a secuirty first, freedom and morality second mindset. So if they ever want to convince the intelligence agencies they're not a national security threat and should be aloud a normal life and/or to convince the intelligence agencies to dial back the evilness of their research programs, they have to find the Beast(s) responsible for teaching the intelligence community and deal with them. (Naturally, said Beast is a hydra <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> That's just one example. The important thing is that their motivation for hunting beasts ties into their backstory and their ongoing recovery from their past.<br /> <br /> <br /> The second question is how do they liberate satellite groups? The Merrik Institute is powerful in dreams, but attacking what's bound to be a guarded institution run by the USA government is no easy feat. And security will only increase after every attack.<br /> <br /> I'd actually consider replacing this entirely - or at least making it a footnote under The Enemy as something they do, but only rarely because it's hard and often involves a trade with another Conspiracy. For a replacement, I'd say that by exploring the dreamworld they can find likely candidates for recuritment by the constantly remaining institute's successors. They coach them on how to fool the tests; but sometimes when there's trouble (usually a Beast) prowling the local dreamscape the candidates insist on learning to protect themselves. This would let you have a Cells that's basically the cast of Nightmare of Elm Street - I.E. They still live with their parents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Enemy</b><br /> <br /> I particularly liked the Changeling there. The Institute and Changelings have a lot in common so it's good to see that acknowledged like this. The bit about Beasts I've covered above.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hunters</b><br /> <br /> A good set of diversity here, it does well to show that there's more reactions to the procedures than angst. I felt that the AI wiz could have tied into the 80s Conspiracy angle more, rather than being an introverted AI researcher, someone who investigates conspiracy theories and uses tech knowledge from classified blueprints. After all, with the intelligence community after them someone's got to keep the institute one step ahead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Factions</b><br /> <br /> I liked Reformers and Firebrands. I wasn't too sold on Fleshists though. It's not that I disliked with the concept of Fleshists, but rather I felt that Factions are the wrong place for this concept. They aren't a third opinion on the question of whether the Institute should be formalized or remain a decentralized network of cells.<br /> <br /> Perhaps move this concept up to The Enemy section - and use the larger wordcount possibility to tie their prey into the backstory - then make the third Faction one who believes that the Instiute should be disbanded entirely with the members going back to normal life, after they take care of ______ that makes normality impossible.<br /> <br /> <b>Status</b><br /> <br /> It looks fine to me. A quick section on how you gain Status like you'd see in Hunter Core wouldn't go amiss.<br /> <br /> <b>Serotypes </b><br /> <br /> All good.<br /> <br /> <b>The Procedure</b><br /> <br /> An ability for cross reality Teamwork Actions. Solid gold concept, it's really fitting and mechanically it's a very practical ability. It needs the Dramatic Failure / Failure / Success / Exceptional Success results in the write up; or it could be turned into a Merit. A Merit might work better actually, if Failure means that four out of five players are cut off from the action, a Merit has no need for a roll and thus it can avoid that un-fun outcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Dream Avatar</b><br /> <br /> Yep, this sounds like fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Any chance you could bump up the dream-Merits Dots up to 8? That would make it provide the same experience points as it does for Skills/Attributes, and allow easy access to the fun high tier Fighting Styles.<br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral Fetish</b><br /> <br /> Thematically appropriate, and you can have a lot of fun thinking up backstories here. I like it.<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamscaping</b><br /> <br /> Normally I like my Conspiracies to have Endowments that make monsters quake in their boots. Like Setto, which could inspire paranoia about physical contact or haggling in monsters all across Japan just by existing. However the whole teens vs Fready Couger aspect of this group, and their lack of organisation means I think of this group as a Compact anyway. So this lower powered Endowment, which must be combined with Tactics and numbers to take on a Beast feels very appropraite.<br /> <br /> I like it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:33:17-07:00","id":892489,"title":"","content":"I'm jazzed about it. The whole YA fugitives angle is very appropriate, though it does make me wonder about the role of the &quot;real&quot; Merrick. Are they another different hunter group that in parallel acts as an antagonist to the free cells? Or is the work they do entirely unrelated?<br /> <br /> I'm still digesting Dreamscaping, but I love The Procedure, Dream Avatar, and Ephemeral Fetish. If I have any notes I would be in favor of adding potential failure to the Procedure tactic, as even though having it fouled up would be un-fun it would also raise stakes and be appropriate in context. Not that everything has to call back to this one point of reference, but in <i>NoES 3</i> the plan in the final act was to all go in together and roll up on Freddy as a group, but instead they got separated and the stage for the finale was set. I would also suggest that Dream Avatar be allowed to be a little stronger given its fairly narrow application. It may be that it is significantly more potent in conjunction with Dreamscaping than I'm realizing, but were I to play one of these hunters I'd probably be more about the merit than the endowment anyway.<br /> <br /> I also enjoy that The Procedure is potentially available to Null Mysteriis and Cheiron Group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T09:34:18-07:00","id":892582,"title":"","content":"I'm not sold on why they attack Beasts. It feels weird that they'd be forced to fight and then keep doing the fighting. Not unreasonable, but weird.<br /> <br /> My main concern about these guys (other than feeling Dreamshaping is wonky and wordy and could probably be handled with a simpler system) is that they're going to be hard to play in a group. They don't have any way to effect the real world, and they don't really have any way to bring other people along with them for the Hunt. Everyone else sitting around a computer screen or whatever and providing voice with an internet connection style support doesn't seem conducive to an interesting game.<br /> <br /> Also? Kids taken away and experimented on by shadowy government agents who then escaped and are fighting the good fight while being hunted by The Man? Sounds like Deviants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T11:23:33-07:00","id":892643,"title":"","content":"Good guy David, gives us all of those tasty spoilers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, thanks for the Avatar merit! I was about to write something similar for my own homebrew conspiracy, but you saved me the trouble :P Waiting eagerly for that chapter to come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T13:01:05-07:00","id":892719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892582#post892582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sold on why they attack Beasts. It feels weird that they'd be forced to fight and then keep doing the fighting. Not unreasonable, but weird.<br /> <br /> My main concern about these guys (other than feeling Dreamshaping is wonky and wordy and could probably be handled with a simpler system) is that they're going to be hard to play in a group. They don't have any way to effect the real world, and they don't really have any way to bring other people along with them for the Hunt. Everyone else sitting around a computer screen or whatever and providing voice with an internet connection style support doesn't seem conducive to an interesting game.<br /> <br /> Also? Kids taken away and experimented on by shadowy government agents who then escaped and are fighting the good fight while being hunted by The Man? Sounds like Deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nutshell: THe process basically pinged them with a giant flashing billboard telling Beast's Horrors &quot;Hey, big tasty treat, right here!&quot;<br /> <br /> You get mauled enough by something, you kind of start to take it personal, which is how these kids become monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T14:38:05-07:00","id":892785,"title":"","content":"You might want to put in a line about Dream Avatar not being able to purchase itself, otherwise you can just purchase Dream Avatar, use that to get two more Dream Avatars, then use that to get four more Dream Avatars, then use those to get eight more Dream Avatars, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:21:29-07:00","id":892862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892467#post892467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to do a full readthrough of this, like I did for the Japanease ones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dream Avatar</b><br /> <br /> Yep, this sounds like fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Any chance you could bump up the dream-Merits Dots up to 8? That would make it provide the same experience points as it does for Skills/Attributes, and allow easy access to the fun high tier Fighting Styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason I didn't was because it's kind of a huge number, and it's sort of annoying to deal with at the table. I might though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:22:43-07:00","id":892863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892785#post892785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to put in a line about Dream Avatar not being able to purchase itself, otherwise you can just purchase Dream Avatar, use that to get two more Dream Avatars, then use that to get four more Dream Avatars, then use those to get eight more Dream Avatars, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll note that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T22:27:54-07:00","id":893037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892286#post892286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brilliant.<br /> <br /> Though part of me is disappointed that Reformers are more prevalent in Canada than they are in Australia considering Dreamtime stuff, but it's easier to walk to Canada than Australia I suppose...</div> </div> </div> </div>I, on the other hand, positively squealed with excitement, since this group is both in my native country and hits the demographic that I work with professionally. Yes, the Merrick Institute will be very fun to write fiction for. Thanks for the spoilers David! Looks great!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T01:16:26-07:00","id":893127,"title":"","content":"I am absolutely loving this group. Well done! It was a nice touch with the Grimm, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:24:18-07:00","id":893419,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Might not be relevant here, or maybe it is. When they are projecting in dream form, do they count as Goetia? I wonder if they could pull back some of their Dream Abilities into the &quot;real&quot; world by effectively &quot;Claiming&quot; themselves.<br /> <br /> That's probably crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-18-2016, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:37:25-07:00","id":893427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=893419#post893419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Might not be relevant here, or maybe it is. When they are projecting in dream form, do they could as effectively Goetia? I wonder if they could pull back some of their Dream Abilities into the &quot;real&quot; world by effectively &quot;Claiming&quot; themselves.<br /> <br /> That's probably crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like a neat endgame merit for them, at least. Some sort of &quot;super mode&quot;, furthering the Deviant parallels? <br /> <br /> Though I'm curious, who can buy Dream Avatar?Can only members of this Conspiracy buy it, can any mortal buy it, is it even available to full supernaturals?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is awesome and so are you. Thank you!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ignore last edit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 05-18-2016, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:28:02-07:00","id":893716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=893427#post893427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sounds like a neat endgame merit for them, at least. Some sort of &quot;super mode&quot;, furthering the Deviant parallels?<br /> <br /> Though I'm curious, who can buy Dream Avatar?Can only members of this Conspiracy buy it, can any mortal buy it, is it even available to full supernaturals?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is awesome and so are you. Thank you!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ignore last edit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say anyone sufficiently tied to their dreams. It is a supernatural Merit. So, it'd be limited to &quot;mortal&quot; characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T17:42:20-07:00","id":893751,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:18:27-07:00","id":894395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=892582#post892582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sold on why they attack Beasts. It feels weird that they'd be forced to fight and then keep doing the fighting. Not unreasonable, but weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said something similar in my read through, that the Begotten need to tie into their backstory a bit more. (I'm tempted to create my own spin on this group - it wouldn't look like the idea in my read through, I've had new ideas - but in all honesty I think I'll keep focusing on Leviathan for now)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:34:23-07:00","id":894461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=894395#post894395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said something similar in my read through, that the Begotten need to tie into their backstory a bit more. (I'm tempted to create my own spin on this group - it wouldn't look like the idea in my read through, I've had new ideas - but in all honesty I think I'll keep focusing on Leviathan for now)</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that they got exposed to ravenous a Beast's Horror going on the hunt on their own accord to develop their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T03:09:14-07:00","id":894643,"title":"","content":"That's not quite the same. By tie in I don't just mean a Beast was there, but that the Beast's behaviour in the backstory parallels the constantly renaming organisation.<br /> <br /> For example one of the test subjects might have unlocked their latent Beast powers (Anakim Tyrant seems fitting) as a result of the experiments, led the escape, and adopted the others as family. However the Institute came to feel that the Tyrant was too similar to the government conspiracy and turned upon him; declaring that they'll never be abused turned abusers and will always stand up for the little guy.<br /> <br /> The idea is to draw similarities between Beasts and the Constantly Renaming Organisation, so that the rich emotional material in the backstory can also be applied to Beasts. Simply having been hurt by Beasts isn't enough, the star of the show in the backstory is the government conspiracy - that's where the emotional goldmine lies so clear links to transfer that emotional richness towards Beasts are needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T19:04:13-07:00","id":895221,"title":"","content":"I love these guys, but they almost feel more like Deviants than Hunters. Their writeup says &quot;run a chronicle about fighting the bastards who did this to you&quot; far more strongly than it says &quot;keep fighting the things you were forced to fight.&quot; Again, they may be in my top three Conspiracies now, but they strike me as Beast hunters by circumstance rather than by creed, and I have to wonder if that's intentional.<br /> <br /> (Don't get me wrong; I'd sooner do a story about fighting a black budget inside the government than one about fighting Beasts. This group screams for a chance to be unlikely allies in a VASCU chronicle, or to be the dirty secret unearthed in a paranoid mortals/Tier 1 thing at its climax).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T07:33:07-07:00","id":896075,"title":"","content":"Do these Hunters use the normal nine attributes while in the Primordial Dream? The Procedure writeup implies their physical bodies are still in the mundane world, so they should be using simplified Power, Resistance, and Finesse, right? In which case Dream Avatar creates an interesting parallel with Beasts, who add 2 attribute dots to their Horror per rank of Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T20:20:47-07:00","id":898545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=896075#post896075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do these Hunters use the normal nine attributes while in the Primordial Dream? The Procedure writeup implies their physical bodies are still in the mundane world, so they should be using simplified Power, Resistance, and Finesse, right? In which case Dream Avatar creates an interesting parallel with Beasts, who add 2 attribute dots to their Horror per rank of Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>We use simplified rules for the dream in Hunter. I don't have the space to give full treatment of Beast style dream rules here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T20:25:00-07:00","id":898549,"title":"","content":"Here's some more content for the Merrick Institute, showing the roles their members might play on the hunt. <br /> <br /> The Merrick Institute <br /> We hunt where nobody else can, or will. <br /> We hunt nightmares. We hunt the truest monsters. <br /> In This Dream<br /> Most of our hunts occur in the dreamscapes. More often than not, that means having one or two members in the dreamscape, and the rest of the team supporting her. <br /> The main member here is the dream warrior. She's not the only essential member, but she's the one that's doing the job we came for. <br /> One member of the team acts as a &quot;teller&quot;, watching monitors and helping the dream warrior do her job. Our monitors on the outside are clearer, more logical than what the dream warrior sees. The monitors cut through the bullshit. Besides, they see from a wider perspective. The dream warrior only sees what's right in front of her. A teller can pan around, and tell her if a beast is creeping up behind her. (Tellers often use Merits such as Small Unit Tactics and Inspiring to support the dream warrior.) <br /> One member usually acts as &quot;pusher&quot;, who runs scientific and mathematical tests on the dream world. The thing about the dream is, it doesn't work like reality that we know. Have you ever watched the cartoon where the animal runs out over the cliff, but doesn't fall until he looks down? That's like the nightmare. Pushers have tools which can move stuff around a little, and monitors which measure and gauge what they push. They can tell you what's hard, soft, hot, cold, sharp, sticky, heavy, illusionary, or whatever. Some groups call them &quot;sandboxers&quot;. (This is represented by the Dreampushing Merit on p. XX). <br /> One cell mate acts as a &quot;puller&quot;, which is to say he stands by with the switch or plug, ready to pull the dream warrior out before the monster kills her. This is a thankless job, because every dream warrior thinks, &quot;I could have taken one more hit. I could have stopped it!&quot; This always ends in argument. But we all know it's an essential job, just one you can never get right. Pullers also act like medics. We can't do a whole lot for a dream warrior, but we can offer a little respite and pick-me-up in the field. (This is represented by the Dream Medic Merit on p. XX).<br /> We have a system. It's good. But, that's just not enough. We need talent, luck, skill, and willpower. We're engaging beasts on their home turf. We can't just kick down a lair door, march in, and shoot the fucker. We do recon missions. We scout. We cripple defenses in advance. We interfere in the beast's feasts so he's hungry when we move in for the kill. We harry, stick, move, and flee. We try to do lasting damage when possible, then duck out before the repercussions. <br /> <br /> Dream Medic (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Intelligence \u2022\u2022\u2022, Medicine \u2022\u2022<br /> Effect: Your character is able to heal and support a person currently in a dream using basic chemicals. To use Dream Medic, your character must have access to the dreaming person's body, and must have access to the necessary chemicals. A chem kit is Availability \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, but can be scavenged from a pharmacy or drug store. In a pinch, she can scrounge one from convenience store pharmaceuticals, but all rolls to administer the medicine are made at -2, and all failures are treated as dramatic failures. <br /> With a kit, your character can administer chems to the dreamer. Roll Intelligence + Medicine + Dream Medic. Successes can be spent on the following, which only affect the character in the dream world. <br /> \u2022 Heal 1 lethal damage, or 2 bashing damage. <br /> \u2022 Give +2 dice to a single dice pool. <br /> \u2022 Give +5 to the next Initiative roll. <br /> \u2022 Give +10 to Speed for a turn. <br /> Successes must be spent in the same scene. The dreamer can spend no more successes in a turn than your character has dots in Dream Medic. <br /> This can be done as many times as you'd like. However, each additional roll made in the same day suffers a cumulative -2 penalty, with no upward limit. Failures cause 1 lethal damage to the character's real world body. Dramatic failures cause 5 damage, and the character falls comatose until all the damage is healed. <br /> <br /> Dreampushing (\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Dream Shaping \u2022<br /> Effect: Your character can enact minor influence on the dream world, from without. She cannot make physical attacks, but has fine manipulation. Essentially, if it could be done with hands, but not with arms, she can handle it. These hypothetical, invisible &quot;hands&quot; move up to half her Speed per turn (but must stay within arms' reach of each other), and act with an effective Strength equal to her Intelligence, and Dexterity equal to her Wits. The &quot;hands&quot; are essentially invincible, but relay sensory information to your character. For example, she knows if she touches something hot, even if it cannot burn her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T20:48:25-07:00","id":898573,"title":"","content":"These look fun. Dreampushing seems like a useful way to contribute without actually going in.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm assuming that Dream Shaping does not count as something the Dreampusher can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 05-24-2016, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T20:55:00-07:00","id":898576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=898573#post898573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These look fun. Dreampushing seems like a useful way to contribute without actually going in.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm assuming that Dream Shaping does not count as something the Dreampusher can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>My default assumption is that yes, you can use Shaping. I'm 50/50 on that, though.<br /> <br /> Also, here's the whole thing, compiled. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10VaWnIXogxWRN7B1xoWiAaMah3ZSxzgdNC_PGOmumCs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10VaWnIXogxWRN7B1xoWiAaMah3ZSxzgdNC_PGOmumCs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10VaWnIXogxWRN7B1xoWiAaMah3ZSxzgdNC_PGOmumCs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/10VaWnIXogxWRN7B1xoWiAaMah3ZSxzgdNC_PGOmumCs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:27:30-07:00","id":899256,"title":"","content":"I must say I do like the expansion about the original nameless organization- and how similar are the Institute for those people the fight against, in the ways of changing identity and always changing and moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:54:00-07:00","id":910143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=898545#post898545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We use simplified rules for the dream in Hunter. I don't have the space to give full treatment of Beast style dream rules here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This worries me. I'm concerned that having multiple rule sets for dream form is going to cause issues down the road. If this is how it has to be then at some point we're going to need some way to determine which to use or how to resolve conflicts between them. So far Mage and Beast use one set and Hunter and Changeling use another and these sets are incompatible with one another, mainly in respect to how damage is handled. For example: in Beast and Mage damage taken in dream form is not carried over to the waking world and death merely results in the Soul Shocked condition. In Changeling, and now hunter, damage taken in the dream <b>is</b> carried over and then downgraded one step and dying in the dream can kill you. And this is before taking into account that how health is calculated is different between the two rule sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:39:17-07:00","id":910494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=910143#post910143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This worries me. I'm concerned that having multiple rule sets for dream form is going to cause issues down the road. If this is how it has to be then at some point we're going to need some way to determine which to use or how to resolve conflicts between them. So far Mage and Beast use one set and Hunter and Changeling use another and these sets are incompatible with one another, mainly in respect to how damage is handled. For example: in Beast and Mage damage taken in dream form is not carried over to the waking world and death merely results in the Soul Shocked condition. In Changeling, and now hunter, damage taken in the dream <b>is</b> carried over and then downgraded one step and dying in the dream can kill you. And this is before taking into account that how health is calculated is different between the two rule sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>You use the rukes for whatever game you're playing, just the same way that Hunter doesn't reprint any Disciplines or Powers or that Mage 2e treats weird things as &quot;like spirits but they aren't really.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T22:47:01-07:00","id":910583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=910494#post910494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You use the rukes for whatever game you're playing, just the same way that Hunter doesn't reprint any Disciplines or Powers or that Mage 2e treats weird things as &quot;like spirits but they aren't really.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought avoiding these kinds of situations was a design goal for NWoD/CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T02:32:58-07:00","id":910650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=910583#post910583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought avoiding these kinds of situations was a design goal for NWoD/CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter specifically always played fast and loose with other splats rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:48:39-07:00","id":910740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=910583#post910583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought avoiding these kinds of situations was a design goal for NWoD/CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you also don't want to have a situation where a necessary subsystem is printed in a book from another game line that you don't own, nor should you have to reprint it in its entirely every time something references it. So in edge cases like this you use a simplified version.<br /> <br /> Besides, its &quot;dream combat.&quot; If anything is going to be fast and loose its application its going to be something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 06-09-2016, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T20:11:22-07:00","id":912056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=910740#post910740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you also don't want to have a situation where a necessary subsystem is printed in a book from another game line that you don't own, nor should you have to reprint it in its entirely every time something references it. So in edge cases like this you use a simplified version.<br /> <br /> Besides, its &quot;dream combat.&quot; If anything is going to be fast and loose its application its going to be something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. If I wanted to include the relevant rules in their entirety, it'd take half the word count I get for the book in entirety. Reprinting them would be kind of absurd. So I'm doing a VERY simple hack, like short sidebar level, and saying that if you want to use more complicated subsystems, to check Beast or Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T03:47:03-07:00","id":912719,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a>, mind if I post up my own tweaks on the backstory? I've got an idea to thematically tie Beasts into the backstory a bit tighter that's buzzing around my brain asking to be posted. (the one on page 2)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:09:34-07:00","id":913157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=912719#post912719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a>, mind if I post up my own tweaks on the backstory? I've got an idea to thematically tie Beasts into the backstory a bit tighter that's buzzing around my brain asking to be posted. (the one on page 2)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:55:41-07:00","id":913175,"title":"","content":"Wait, there's going to be a Mortal Remains-style thing about Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T06:51:22-07:00","id":913361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=913157#post913157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I hope you like it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Conspiracy: The Merrick Institute</span></span><br /> &quot;We're kin? I guess that makes you the abusive dad.&quot;<br /> <br /> In January 1987, Epsilon Protocol became Strunk Developments. In July 1987, Strunk Developments became Merrick Research. Just about every six months, this United States government shadow organization changes its name and burns all paper trails. They destroy all unnecessary research notes, move facilities, and salt and burn. Researchers only know the bare minimum they have to, and undergo excessive and traumatic debriefings if and when they leave.<br /> <br /> This organization, Merrick Research we'll call it even though there's no record of that name existing, exists to tap into the subconscious power of the human mind. Another group had similar goals, developing a method called the Wintergreen Process. The Merrick practice, which has no formal name, is far more dangerous, far more damaging, but ultimately far more dramatic in its effects. Successful inductees become able to walk through a parallel world borne of human nightmares. A collective unconscious if you will, where a long walk could take you into your enemies dreams where his secrets are laid bare. That is, if you could avoid the monsters living upon the path. <br /> <br /> Merrick &quot;inducts&quot; children who meet certain very rare criteria in standardized tests filtered through the public school system. When these rare combinations of correct and incorrect results come up, Merrick's surrogates offer parents lucrative scholarship packages, and &quot;enrollment in an elite school&quot;. On occasion, parents who refuse these advances disappear, their children ending up in Merrick laboratories anyway.<br /> <br /> The children, usually right on the cusp of adolescence, undergo terrifying chemical, psychological, and physical trials made to force specific and targeted growth inside their brains. These trials often kill the subjects, and almost always leave them permanently damaged on a physical or psychological level. Most remain institutionalized for the entirety of their short lives. Some are inducted into military programs.<br /> <br /> At least, that was the case until 2013. Standardised tests are never perfectly accurate, and tests delivered through unwitting pawns are less so. A false positive brought a student whose soul contained a sleeping giant into the laboratory, and when the experiments woke that giant the results were brutal. Only the imprisoned subjects and a few scientists known to help the teens against their captors survived. They all followed their new leader when he showed them the way to enter a dreamscape in body and invited them to shelter in his castle.<br /> <br /> But a giant must have a giant appetite, the teens caught their leader torturing a hapless dreamer in a hidden corner of his castle. The giant claimed he was doing it for the dreamer's own good, to help him become stronger. Those were the wrong words, for they were the same words the institute so often used to justify their experiments.<br /> <br /> Furious, the teens combined their powers over dreams and held the giant fast. They made him promise to never do something so horrible again and when he broke that promise they made a choice. They tore down the castle knowing it was the last place that they would ever be safe.<br /> <br /> Together they made an oath to make the best use of whatever time they had before the intelligence community found. To always be there for powerless victims like they themselves once where, and to never become the like the monsters who made them what they are, even if it cost their very lives.<br /> <br /> Then, they scattered and hid. Now, they've divided into loosely organized cells all over North America (and at least a couple have snuck abroad), and they scramble from place to place, building and scrapping the technology to support their cause, as they evade the intelligence community's inevitable approach. They spread warnings about standardised tests through the internet and dreams and sometimes they induct candidates themselves, but only those who insist after repeated warnings.<br /> <br /> They call themselves the Merrick Institute, despite not being an institute in any formal sense, as a sort of defiant mockery of their past captors.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Enemy</span><br /> The Merrick dreamers' are constantly pursued by the intelligence community and that means they need to defend themselves. Their abilities mostly exist within dreams but dreams can do a lot of good: Warning potential targets, stealing and publishing government secrets, they can even make teens vanish from their cells and take them to safety through the dreamscape. Though that last one requires calling in a favor from more powerful allies.<br /> <br /> But the Institute has sworn not to become like their former captors. Morality is too high a price for security, and so they they don't just protect their own. The Institute considers themselves the enemies of all tyrants and abusers, and since they hunt tyrants within dreams they Hunt Beasts. into the Merrick dreamers' primary target. The institute considers Beasts' to be tyrants abusing the powerless, with a justification that's both so flimsy it's not worth thinking about and offensive on a personal level.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, dreamers run afoul of changelings and other strangeness within dreams. One dreamer found herself abducted by a terrifying, alien entity from beyond her dreams. She eventually escaped, but was forever changed. Her flesh bore the words of the stories she remembered to help her escape. She taught the institute much about travelling within dreamscapes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Hunters</span><br /> A Slasher preyed upon your town, attacking people in their sleep and inflicting fatal wounds that appeared upon their bodies. So when the Merrick Institute came to warn you about the government you didn't let them leave until they'd given you more than a warning. It was a rough time for the Institute, they could only give you blueprints. You were way over your head, five teens breaking into the school science lab to recreate black ops medical experiments but you made it work. You defeated the monster and afterwards; having a safe home, a good family, and no spooks on your trail means you have a lot of time to pay the favor forward.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some post write up commentary.<br /> <br /> <br /> I had three goals with this:<br /> <br /> 1) Promote Beasts from secondary characters into primary characters within the backstory. Being forced to fight monsters can leave you with a hatred of monsters; but thematically the monsters will always be in the shadow of whoever forced you to fight \u2013 hence why we had comments saying they feel more like Deviants than hunters. It is my hope that giving a Beast a key place in their origin story will help rectify that.<br /> <br /> 2) Make the Merrick Institute present a conflicting point of view on one of Beast's themes. I felt family works best. The institute are what TvTropes calls a &quot;Secret Project Refugee Family&quot;. Beast has a theme of \u201cYou Don't Choose Your Family\u201d, so contrasting it was easy. I made it clear that the Merrick Institute do choose their family. They have a philosophical belief in opposing tyranny and standing up for the little guy, if you don't share their philosophy you're out the family.<br /> <br /> I actually spotted a second point of contrast when I was writing it, and made sure to include that too. One of Beast's primary justification for feeding is that they don't have a choice. The Merrick Institute are also in a tight corner, with spooks breathing down their neck. However the Merrick Institute believe that they always have a choice. They decided death was better than becoming a monster.<br /> <br /> 3) Add an extra example to the Hunter section explaining how the cast of Freddy Kruger, that is teenagers with a fairly mundane backstory, might become a part of the institute.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T07:53:06-07:00","id":914826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute?p=912056#post912056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. If I wanted to include the relevant rules in their entirety, it'd take half the word count I get for the book in entirety. Reprinting them would be kind of absurd. So I'm doing a VERY simple hack, like short sidebar level, and saying that if you want to use more complicated subsystems, to check Beast or Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to ask the same thing, because I was confused by the lack of rules for Dream Form. I can understand not wanting to fill up your wordcount with those rules, but taking the relevant parts of the Mage rules for Dream Form, taking out the Mage specific stuff, adding the Soul Shocked Condition and doing no futher cutting gets me 298 words. That's with some room left for further shortening.<br /> Doesn't seem that much, might even be possible to shorten it enough to fit into a sidebar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}